" on the column that holds it, naming the table and column it points at (a primary key or a unique column of the same type), and onDelete where it matters. A many-to-many relation is its own table with a foreign key to each side. A key over several columns together goes in the table's \"uniques\".\n- Every table has a primary key. Use the names the code will use for the tables and columns.\n- Model what is stored, not what the API returns: a field worked out on each request has no column.\n- No task writes contracts/data-model.yaml: it is the factory's file. Put the entities, the database setup and any migration in the fileScope of the first task that uses each table.\n\nRepository map:\nApp.Api/AppDb.cs\n  class AppDb\nApp.Api/Program.cs\n  class Program\nApp.Api/SeedData.cs\n  class SeedData\n    void Run(AppDb db)\nApp.Tests/HealthTests.cs\n  class HealthTests\n    Task ApiIsUp()","tools":["read_file","search","repo_map"],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"The App PostgreSQL database is fresh and empty; startup `EnsureCreated` creates the schema, and no migration or backfill is required.\",\n  \"Interpret sample-row expectations as at least two rows per empty application table where applicable; use plausible schema-valid values and contract examples where available, with association rows referencing valid seeded records.\",\n  \"OAuth client ID, client secret, and redirect URI are supplied through deployment configuration or secrets for each environment.\",\n  \"The availability email operation dispatches through a configured email delivery service; the contract does not prescribe a provider or protocol.\"\n ],\n \"critic\": [],\n \"lint\": [\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L1 ids\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L2 req-ac\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L3 ears\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L4 vague\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L5 nfr\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L6 scope\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L8 anchors\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L9 size\",\n   \"details\": \"This spec has 27 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.\",\n   \"passed\": false\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L10 trace\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L11 observable\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L12 literals\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"metric\": \"22 of 22 contract operationIds are exposed and pass contract-level HTTP checks.\",\n   \"text\": \"All operations declared by the locked OpenAPI contract are implemented with the contract's request, response, and security definitions.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"Native iOS and Android client applications and employee-facing product screens.\",\n  \"Physical license-plate-recognition camera capture, continuous vehicle monitoring, indicator hardware, and device integrations beyond the documented `POST /api/entrance/verify` HTTP operation.\",\n  \"Corporate-directory synchronization beyond the identity and profile behavior defined by the OpenAPI contract.\",\n  \"Automated weekly report generation and scheduled stakeholder email delivery beyond the documented report and notification API operations.\",\n  \"Push-notification delivery and automatic release-time scheduling beyond documented contract operations.\",\n  \"Parking policies and external workflows not explicitly defined by `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n  \"Database migration, legacy-data backfill, and preservation of pre-existing App database contents; this implementation assumes a fresh database and uses startup `EnsureCreated`.\",\n  \"Web or mobile employee-facing product screens are excluded from this API-repository change.\"\n ],\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"OAuth client ID and redirect URI are configured for deployment.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains an `authorizationUrl` reflecting the configured client ID and redirect URI and a non-empty `state`.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/auth/google/authorization`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Required Google OAuth configuration or authorization service is unavailable.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 503 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/auth/google/authorization`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a client requests `GET /api/auth/google/authorization`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement `getGoogleAuthorization` according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`, constructing the Google Workspace authorization URL from deployment-configured OAuth values.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-3\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid Google Workspace authorization code and matching state identify an eligible Folio3 employee.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response session contains `id`, `employeeId`, `employeeName`, `corporateEmail`, `role`, and `accessToken`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends `POST /api/auth/sign-in` with `authorizationCode` and `state`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"OAuth values are configured and a valid authorization code is submitted.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The request sent to Google's token endpoint contains the configured client ID, client secret, redirect URI, authorization code, and state.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API exchanges the code with Google Workspace.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The sign-in request has a missing, invalid, or mismatched state or code, an ineligible identity, or Google service is unavailable.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400 for an invalid request, 401 for an unaccepted identity, or 503 for an unavailable service, and each error response contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends `POST /api/auth/sign-in`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a client submits `POST /api/auth/sign-in`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement `signIn` according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`, exchanging the authorization code with Google Workspace using deployment-configured OAuth values and accepting only eligible Folio3 Workspace identities.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-3\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid bearer session identifies an employee with a profile and registered vehicles.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response profile contains the contract's required employee fields, including `id`, `employeeId`, `employeeName`, `corporateEmail`, `dedicatedParking`, `assignedFloor`, `assignedSpace`, and the employee's `vehicles` list.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/employees/me`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The bearer token is absent or invalid, the identity lacks access, or no employee profile exists.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401, 403, or 404 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/employees/me`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/employees/me`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `getMyEmployeeProfile` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session and available App database identify an employee.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response dashboard contains the contract's required fields, including `officeDate`, `timezone`, `releaseTime`, `assignedSpace`, `spaceStatus`, `availableSpaces`, `registeredVehicle`, `workingDays`, and `workingDayRule`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/parking/dashboard`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request has no valid bearer token.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/parking/dashboard`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/parking/dashboard`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `getParkingDashboard` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The bearer session identifies an employee with dedicated parking and the submitted `officeDate` is today in the office timezone and releasable.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response release contains `officeDate`, `space`, `status`, `claimableAt`, and `auditEvents`, including a `Released` action.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee posts the today-release request.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated, the employee is not eligible to release dedicated parking, or the release conflicts with the current parking state.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401, 403, or 409 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/parking/releases/today`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `POST /api/parking/releases/today`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `releaseTodaysSpace` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies an employee with registered vehicles.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response `vehicles` list contains only that employee's vehicles with contract fields, including `id`, `plate`, `make`, `model`, `color`, and `active`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/vehicles`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request has no valid bearer token.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/vehicles`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/vehicles`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `listMyVehicles` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session and vehicle input with a valid plate and optional make, model, and color are supplied.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response vehicle record contains `id`, `plate`, `make`, `model`, `color`, and `active` set to true.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee posts the vehicle input to `/api/vehicles`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The vehicle input is invalid, the request is unauthenticated, or the plate conflicts with an existing record.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400, 401, or 409 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/vehicles`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `POST /api/vehicles`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `registerVehicle` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies an employee with saved releases and audit events.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response `releases` list contains only that employee's releases with contract fields, including `id`, `officeDate`, `space`, `status`, `claimableAt`, and `auditEvents`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/parking/releases`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request has no valid bearer token.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/parking/releases`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/parking/releases`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `listMyReleases` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies a dedicated-parking holder and `officeDates` contains one or more valid dates within the next 30 calendar days.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response `releases` list contains the saved dates and a `Scheduled` audit event for each release.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee posts the schedule to `/api/parking/releases`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The schedule request is malformed, the employee is not eligible, or dates violate the contract's date rules.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400, 403, or 422 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/parking/releases`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `POST /api/parking/releases`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `scheduleParkingReleases` operation for one or more dates within the next 30 calendar days according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The bearer session owns an unclaimed scheduled release identified by `releaseId`.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200, the response release status is `Cancelled`, and its `auditEvents` list includes scheduling and cancellation events.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee deletes `/api/parking/releases/{releaseId}`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The release does not exist, belongs to another employee, has already been claimed, or the request is unauthenticated.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 404, 403, 409, or 401 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client deletes `/api/parking/releases/{releaseId}`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `DELETE /api/parking/releases/{releaseId}`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `cancelParkingRelease` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session exists and office capacity, release time, and current parking allocations are configured.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains `officeDate`, `timezone`, `availableSpaces`, `releaseTime`, and a `floors` list with `floor`, `freeSpaces`, and `totalSpaces`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/parking/availability`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request has no valid bearer token.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/parking/availability`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/parking/availability`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `getParkingAvailability` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies an eligible employee, the selected registered vehicle belongs to that employee, and a space is claimable for `officeDate`.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response contains allocated `floor`, `space`, `plate`, `officeDate`, `status`, `entryStatus`, `floorCapacity`, `allocationRule`, and `authorizationScope` fields.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee posts `vehicleId` and `officeDate` to `/api/parking/claims`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Two eligible employees attempt to claim the last available space for the same office date concurrently.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The responses contain exactly one status 201 and one conflict status 409, and the successful response contains one allocated space.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employees submit claims concurrently.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The request is invalid or unauthenticated, the employee is ineligible, the vehicle or date is not eligible, or no space remains available.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400, 401, 403, 409, or 422 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/parking/claims`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `POST /api/parking/claims`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `claimParkingSpace` operation, allocating a claimable temporary space using the submitted registered vehicle, according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies an employee with an active temporary allocation for today.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains the allocation's required `ParkingClaim` fields, including `floor`, `space`, `plate`, `officeDate`, and `entryStatus`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/parking/claims/today`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The employee has no temporary allocation for today or the request has no valid bearer token.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 404 or 401 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values when an error response is returned.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/parking/claims/today`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/parking/claims/today`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `getTodaysParkingClaim` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The bearer session owns an existing claim that can be cancelled.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains the contract's `ParkingClaim` fields, including `id` and the cancellation outcome status.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee deletes `/api/parking/claims/{claimId}`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The claim does not exist, belongs to another employee, cannot be cancelled in its current state, or the request is unauthenticated.\",\n     \"id\":